{% extends '@layout/default.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Scientia Mobile licensed its Wurfl Cloud PHP library to DotKernel 1.6{% endblock %}

{% block page_title %}
    <div class="wrap">
        <div class="post-hero">
            <a href="{{ url('page::blog') }}" class="breadcrumb-back">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M15 18l-6-6 6-6"/></svg>
                Back to Blog
            </a>
            <div><span class="eyebrow">Dotkernel</span></div>
            <h1>{{ article.title }}</h1>
            <div class="post-meta">
                <span class="text-muted small">
                    By <a href="{{ path('page::author-resource', {slug: article.author.slug}) }}" class="fw-bold link-dark text-decoration-none">{{ article.author.name }}</a>
                    &nbsp;.&nbsp; {{ article.postDate|date('M d, Y') }}
                </span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
    <div class="wrap post-body-wrap">
        <div class="post-layout">

            {{ include('@partial/left-menu.html.twig') }}

            <article class="article">
                <div class="entry">
In the DotKernel version 1.6.0 , released on May 16th, 2012 we have removed the GPL'ed WURFL PHP library , as the code it was obsolete anyway and also the structure of the XML file was changed.

Instead , we implemented the <a title="Scientia Mobile" href="http://www.scientiamobile.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Scientia Mobile's </a>WURFL Cloud PHP  library .

<!--more-->

Instructions about how to signup for a free account , and how to setup your API key can be found <a title="Mbile Devices in DotKernel" href="http://www.dotkernel.com/dotkernel/detecting-mobile-devices-in-dotkernel-1-6/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">here .</a>

In the near future, we will create a template in Wurfl Cloud API control panel,  at Scientia Mobile,  ready to be used in DotKernel implementations.

Also, we got a special license, please read the file:

<a href="http://websvn.dotkernel.net/filedetails.php?repname=DotKernel&amp;path=%2Ftrunk%2Flibrary%2FWurflCloud%2FLICENSE.txt" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">dotkernel/library/WurflCloud/LICENSE.txt</a> and notice Dotkernel mention
<blockquote class="blockquote border-start border-4 ps-3 text-muted my-3">License is non-transferable, conditioned, limited to the version
received and to the use and distribution of this software only in connection
with the <strong>Dotkernel</strong> software framework, and does not allow making derivative works
even when the source code is provided or the language is an interpreted one
and regardless of whether the code is not obfuscated.</blockquote>
&nbsp;
                </div>

                {{ include('@partial/post-nav.html.twig') }}
            </article>

        </div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
